    "created_at": "2019-06-03T14:42:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-06-03T14:42:02Z",
    "body": "In https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#playing-the-media-resource there's this bit:\r\n> When the current playback position of a media element changes (e.g. due to playback or seeking), the user agent must run the time marches on steps.\r\n\r\nThis is what should cause cue rendering to be updated when the time changes, whether paused or not and whether the show poster flag is set or not. @alastor0325 does this explain the behavior you saw when testing, or have I misunderstood some aspect of your question/suggestion?\r\n\r\ncc @fsoder",
